# Everything here is excluded from the build context. Keeping it tight is not only about image
# size: a stale bin/ or obj/ copied into the container makes the in-container build pick up
# host-built artefacts for a different RID and fail in confusing ways.

# --- build output --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/TestResults/

# --- version control and IDE state ----------------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.github/
.vs/
.idea/
*.suo
*.user
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates

# --- local-only configuration and secrets ---------------------------------------------------------
# appsettings.Development.json is gitignored and holds the developer's real connection string and
# RSA keypair. It must never be baked into an image: configuration comes from VORTEX__ environment
# variables instead (see docker-compose.yml).
appsettings.Development.json
appsettings.Production.json
**/appsettings.Development.json
**/appsettings.Production.json
**/secrets.json
.env
.env.*

# --- runtime state --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
logs/
plugins/
assets/

# --- container artefacts themselves ---------------------------------------------------------------
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.*.yml

# --- front end -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The dashboard SPA is committed pre-built under Vortex.Dashboard.API/Assets and embedded as a
# resource by the .NET build, so the Vite sources and node_modules are never needed to compile.
**/node_modules/
Vortex.Dashboard.Web/dist/

# --- not needed to compile --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# docs/ and tools/ contain no project referenced by Vortex.Main; tools/catalog_converter alone
# carries tens of megabytes of sample SQL/JSON. Only `dotnet publish` runs in the image — the
# VortexCloudQualityGate / VortexCloudAiGovernanceCheck targets (which do read docs/patterns) are
# run on a developer machine or in CI, never here.
docs/
tools/
